      "result": "All 11 checklist items have been tested and recorded, with progress confirming **complete: true**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI performed a full QA pass against the live app at http://localhost:7063/, covering the homepage list, category/detail views, and the panorama hotspot flow.\n\n**Result: 11/11 PASS**\n\nKey observations that grounded the verdicts:\n- **FT-1/FT-4/CS-7**: Homepage lists 8 heritage items, each tagged with exactly one category (民俗活动/传统美术/传统表演/传统工艺); category filter correctly narrowed results (8 → 2 for 传统工艺).\n- **FT-2/FT-3/CS-8/CS-9**: Clicking \"了解详情\" navigates to a dedicated detail page (e.g. `/heritage/spring-festival`) showing title, region, inscription year, full description, and an image gallery with working thumbnail switching.\n- **FT-5**: Opened the 苏绣 hotspot overlay in the panorama view → navigated to its detail page via \"查看详情\" → used browser back → the panorama and the exact same hotspot overlay (title, images, description) were fully restored.\n- **FT-6**: Observed two explicit UX prompts — a hotspot loading progress indicator (\"正在加载热点... (3/8)\") in the panorama, and a \"图片加载失败\" fallback message when the 春节 detail page's primary image failed to load.\n- **IX-10**: List view (grid/cards) and detail view (breadcrumb + hero image + info panel) are structurally and visually distinct.\n- **CT-11**: All 8 items (春节, 端午龙舟, 剪纸, 京剧, 昆曲, 书法, 苏绣, 宜兴紫砂) are genuine, well-documented Chinese ICH items with historically accurate descriptions and regions.\n\nOne implementation nuance worth flagging (not a failure, since the app still functioned correctly): panorama hotspots continuously reposition in real time, which made Playwright's native click-stability check time out — I had to trigger clicks via `dispatchEvent`/direct DOM `.click()` in `browser_evaluate`. This is consistent with the stated requirement that \"the panoramic perspective and anchor point positions are calculated in real time and must not pause,\" so it reflects intended behavior rather than a defect.",
